WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
<b>2</b> Weeks until the <b>Ezonoo Festival</b>

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:03.700
All right.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:09.140
Pork Soup Café

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:06.740
Get cracking with the Ezonoo 
Festival preparations!

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.830
'Kay!

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.080
I'm game with the whole 
pork soup café thing,

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.700
but it's kinda sad to only 
have that on the menu.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.610
Let's add fried chicken as a snack item!

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:18.390
There are many kinds of pork soup.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:20.140
My family uses barley miso.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.330
Barley miso goes well with pork.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.420
Mine uses blended miso 
with ginger and butter.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:29.310
How about letting people compare different 
pork soup variations across Japan?

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.170
Like golden pork soup using 
high-quality tenderloin!

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:33.830
W-W-Wait!

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.850
You guys need to think about the budget!

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.760
Okay. Hachiken, you manage the budget.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.260
Why me?

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:43.180
You're the only one who 
can do that sort of thing!

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.610
Fine.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:53.030
Hachiken Akeno Hachiken Hachiken Hachiken Inada Hachiken Hachiken Hachiken

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:26.780
Ezonoo Festival 
<b>Small Event Planning{Z: No idea how renderer-san will deal with this. My guess is NG.}</b>

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:28.110
You're better 
at it! 
(Yoda) 

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:28.110
Check out 
Maro's jumps 
(Maruyama)

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:28.120
Show off how 
super cool horses are!! 
(Hachiken)

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:25.170
At the Ezonoo Festival,

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:29.600
I'd like us to show our horsemanship off
 to our visitors in competition format!

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:33.620
<b>Fall Chapter Episode 5
Hachiken 
Has His Hands Full</b>

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.390
I'm sure you're all busy with 
entrance exams and job hunting,

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:36.090
but we're just not good enough to 
show off how awesome horses are...

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.590
So please help us!

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:40.510
If you all insist.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:42.980
I guess I'll pitch in
 for my dear underclassmen!

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.090
It'll be a nice break from job hunting!

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.350
Yeah, right! You said that job hunting
wouldd be a nice break from horses!

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:50.750
What about you?

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.260
My final competition was a rout!

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.110
It's time for a revenge match!

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.100
Yay!

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.920
Thank you!

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.610
What's left?

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:02.610
Banba?

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.220
You're trying to do a Ban'ei 
horse race at the Ezonoo Festival?

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:08.120
There won't be any gambling!

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:12.600
But a sight-seeing carriage ride or something 
would be more popular with visitors.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:16.850
We'd like to make a 200-meter 
long course with two hills,

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.130
but that might be too—

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.300
Why not?

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.360
The fodder corn fields 
aren't being used, right?

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:23.500
Yeah.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.310
Go ahead. Just even out 
the field after the event.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.060
So, how many hectares do you need?

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.440
Oh, that wasn't even in our sights...

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.390
Two, no, three hectares, please!

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:36.400
We want enough space for practice!

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.770
Field 3 should fit the bill.

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:40.370
It's close to the main school building,

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.010
so it'll be easy to attract spectators.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.110
Thank you!

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:48.450
Livestock Management Building

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.630
Land secured!

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:47.160
Next...

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.430
Hey, Uncle?

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.490
It's me, Aki. Are you busy right now?

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.360
I have a favor to ask...

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.660
Yeah, I talked to the teachers already.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:58.910
Yeah.

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:00.350
Yeah...

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.060
Thanks, Uncle!

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.000
Sure thing.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.730
I haven't used this in a long while,

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.430
so it looks kind of shabby.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.790
This takes me back!

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:15.330
Back when we were kids,

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:18.560
we used to do these at 
festivals and local races.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:23.360
I got a ride once from my 
grandfather on his lumber sled.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.110
Who'll be the rider?

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:30.260
Me!

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:33.250
Grandpa taught me a little bit.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.500
It's not something you can do 
by the seat of your pants!

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.630
You're not ready yet!

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:39.810
Aw...

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:47.850
"Yet" means it depends 
on practice, right?

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:48.820
What?

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.360
Safety comes first,

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.630
so if you decide that it wouldn't 
be safe for Mikage-san, {addressing the uncle}

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:55.810
I'll arrange for another rider.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:58.270
Do you want to try?

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:01.950
Yes!

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.240
Thank you.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:09.940
You really light up whenever 
horses are involved.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:11.410
Oh, really?

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:15.620
You really should work 
with horses as a career.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:21.820
Sure, that'd make me happy,

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:24.210
but I have to carry on the family business.

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:28.970
We have our own horses, 
so I can still have fun!

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:32.710
I don't want to fight with my 
folks about my career, either.

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:33.930
I'll be fine!

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:37.900
<b>Ooezo Agricultural High School Dormitory for Future Agriculture Managers</b>

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:37.900
<i>"Don't want to fight," huh?</i>

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:41.140
<i>I wonder if she's been holding her feelings back</i>

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:44.310
<i>because of her family's business.</i>

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.570
I'll be fine!

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.920
Nishikawa, you're good with 
farm equipment, right?

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:53.200
Sure.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:56.690
People are going to take rides on them?

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:59.380
Yeah, so I want them to 
get a proper inspection

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.320
and repaint them so they look better.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.320
What color?

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.670
Let me think...

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:07.310
Something that people will enjoy...

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:09.390
Okay, I'll think of something.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:11.140
Thanks!

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:13.520
I'm sorry to ask you this when you're busy...

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:16.850
but I just really want to make it work!

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:20.310
Don't worry. I'll give it my best shot!

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:23.810
But in exchange, help me 
out with my event, too.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:25.530
Sure, I'd be happy to!

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.060
Okay, okay.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:32.870
I'll take you on a walk right away.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.280
Hachiken!

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:36.530
Sakuragi-sensei was asking for you.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:38.910
You're in charge of the budget 
and the schedule, right?

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:40.340
Oh, crap!

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:43.000
He told me to come by before coming here.

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:45.590
Oops, I gotta walk Vice Prez, too.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:46.830
Walk?

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:48.200
I'll do it.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.140
Really?

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:50.630
Thanks a million!

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:57.630
Hachiken's also in charge 
of our class's small event?

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:59.800
He's a workaholic.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:01.350
I hope he's okay...

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.270
Good job!

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:09.730
What's going on?

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:11.440
Are they doing something out on the farms?

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.050
It's the equestrian club.

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:21.250
And here I thought we were the 
last ones to wrap up today.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:22.570
What's this?

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:24.250
A motocross course?

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.500
We're making a Banba race course.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.200
Banba, as in Ban'ei race course?

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:30.540
Looks hardcore.

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:33.790
The teachers got all nostalgic about 
the local races that used to happen

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:35.190
and went all in.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:40.700
Even Ookawa-san?

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:43.230
He's in Forestry Science, so he got 
volunteered into helping with measurements.

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:45.360
You're really asking a lot!

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.700
I have to find a job!

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.070
You look like you're having a great time.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:50.990
I can't just stand back when 
my underclassmen are pitching in!

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.440
Maybe I'll help, too.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:55.730
Let's go, Matsuyama!

00:07:55.730 --> 00:07:56.580
Seriously?!

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:58.940
Don't worry about it!

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:01.040
You guys have the Hokkaido 
championships coming up, right?!

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:03.510
You guys already spend enough 
time training as it is...

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:05.670
You don't get it, do you, Hachiken?

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:09.370
Baseball muscles and farm 
muscles are different beasts!

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:10.420
You're an idiot.

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:15.940
What's he thinking?

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.000
Is he gonna be okay?

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.050
Icchan's a muscle cyborg.

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:20.220
That's easy for him.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:24.840
But considering what happened to his dad...

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:28.690
I can see why you'd be worried.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.700
But let him have his moment.

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:33.860
Icchan's got a lot of things going on.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:46.830
Whoa, whoa.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:55.760
Hachi,

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:58.610
I finished fixing up one 
of the sleds.

00:08:58.610 --> 00:08:59.720
Really?!

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:01.720
You're a huge help.

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:04.510
Eh, when a buddy comes to you 
for help with something big...

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.440
you can only give it all you've got.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:08.770
Th-This is...

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:11.780
An otaku sled!

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:15.200
What's this "NPK48" about?!

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:26.710
<b>N Nitrogen 
 P Phosphorous 
 K Potassium</b>

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:18.920
Nitrogen, phosphorous, and potassium are 
the three major elements in fertilizer.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:20.790
Didn't you learn that in class?

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:23.390
Wait, you're not a bad hand at drawing.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:26.180
I wanted a paint job that 
would get people's attention.

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:27.260
Oh, wait!

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:28.870
It's not about how it's drawn, but what!

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:31.070
We can't go with this, right, Mikage?!

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:32.910
It looks okay to me...

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:35.570
Don't hold your emotions back, Mikage!

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:37.380
Get mad!

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.770
<i>The sunrise's getting later every day.</i>

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:52.840
<i>Winter's coming.</i>

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:58.080
Maybe we're halfway there...

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:10.080
Master of the apocalypse...

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:13.650
Oh, Hachiken-kun. You're up early.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:15.440
Morning, Hachiken-kun!

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.030
Good morning.

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:20.050
You're pretty cheerful 
for being up so early.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.010
Aren't you tired?

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.890
Well, sure I'm tired.

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.670
But compared to helping out on the family 
farm during peak season, this is easy!

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:28.860
<i>She's lived through hell!</i>

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:33.010
And what're you doing up 
so early, Hachiken-kun?

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:35.030
Morning training isn't for a while.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:40.740
I thought I'd pick up pebbles and 
trash and stuff from the racetrack.

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:45.200
I wouldn't want anything to 
happen to anyone or any horse.

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:50.520
Horses can get sent to the slaughterhouse 
over the smallest thing, you know?

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:55.950
If you're tired, you should rest 
and not push yourself so hard.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.880
Oh, I'm fine.

00:10:58.620 --> 00:10:59.120
Okay!

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:05.350
Yup, I'm fine!

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:08.840
Hachiken!

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:10.220
Wake up!

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:11.440
No, it's fine.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:14.190
Let him sleep.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.860
Hachiken's working hard.

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:19.050
But that's that, and this is different.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:21.320
Hachiken, minus one point.

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:23.270
Equestrian Club 

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:23.270
Racetrack prep 
 Obstacle prep 
 Vice Prez duties 
 Freshman War training

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:25.000
You've got a lot on your plate.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.180
I'll manage somehow.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:32.040
Hachiken, payback time for subbing 
in for dorm cleaning the other day!

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:33.680
Hachi!

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:35.680
Do you remember what you 
gotta do in exchange for

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:36.960
my painting the sled?

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:38.210
Equestrian Club 
 Dairy Science 
 Nishikawa Payback (Agricultural Engineering) 
 Beppu - help with festival exhibit 
 Cattleshed Practicum 
 Brick Oven Manager 

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:38.210
Racetrack prep 
 Obstacle prep 
 Vice Prez duties 
 Freshman War training 
 Manage attendees 
 Shopping 
 Potato harvest

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:40.080
This doesn't look good.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:42.470
Hey, this is way too much...

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:46.180
Come to think of it, we'll have cattleshed 
practicum duties starting next week.

00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:50.310
I guess this is what it means 
to put a festival together...

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:52.250
Festivals are scary...

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:55.060
Nah, it's just your schedule that's weird.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:57.400
If you stay a yes-man, 
you'll die an early death.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:12:00.170
I'm not gonna let anyone add anything 
else to this list, even if they beg!

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:01.190
Never!

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:05.360
Hachiken Yuugo, man in 
charge of the pizza oven!

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:07.410
Come to the student committee office ASAP!

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:11.040
No!

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:11.040
<b>Campus Motto
Defy Logic  Cooperation  Diligence</b>

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:18.460
Thanks for your help yesterday 
with the racetrack, too.

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:19.530
Sure.

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:21.170
Uh, you okay?

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:24.320
I'm going to sleep 
after the festival's over.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:26.630
Sleep till I die.

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:28.890
Oh, Hachiken.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:31.450
That cow's taking a dump.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:38.180
Ugh, why do I get the feeling that 
I'm having to do this a lot lately?

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:39.940
Are you sure you're okay?

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:41.080
Yup.

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:43.030
Just gotta tough it out 
until the festival's over.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:44.830
Here.

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:46.030
Thank you.

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:49.930
Where'd you ditch your mass?

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:51.310
I went on a diet.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:53.660
But I thought you didn't feel 
your best when you're skinny.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:55.040
I asked her to do it.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:59.630
Our club's small event 
is a cow beauty pageant.

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:03.440
So I've been asked to secure 
an audience so that we can

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:06.120
"let the entire world know 
how wonderful Holsteins are"...

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:10.100
But what normal person would 
enjoy watching a cow pageant?!

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:13.670
Securing an audience is impossible!

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:17.920
So I thought we might get some 
people if we focus on the

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:19.900
person who'll be leading the cows...

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:23.860
Oh, so intense!

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:29.240
I agreed in exchange for 5,000 yen worth
 of Ezonoo Festival food tickets.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:33.050
It's just like you to hit the 
target right on the deadline.

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:35.500
You should stay that way forever.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:36.400
No way.

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:37.710
I'd pass out from anemia.

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:40.170
Here's the shopping list.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:42.050
Okay, off I go!

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:46.550
Crap!

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:48.700
I'm going to the farm!

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:52.180
Hachiken, to the farm.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:53.350
Hachiken 
 Farm

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:56.060
<b>Potato Picking</b>

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:56.060
Choose your own 
 <b>100 yen/2</b>kg 
 Agricultural Science 
Department 1-C

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:01.520
What a disaster.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.250
Let me give it another try.

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.820
Can I do something else?

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.120
Can you clear away the stalks?

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:15.950
I had no idea most of these
 aren't good enough to go to market.

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:17.260
Is it so strange?

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:18.390
They're living things.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:20.500
It'd be strange if they all looked the same.

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:23.130
When you let customers pick and choose,

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.760
they leave behind misshapen ones like these.

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:28.630
Yeah, even though they all taste the same.

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:27.920
Misshapen...

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:31.000
<i>They tried to grow bigger, 
but just couldn't.</i>

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.280
<i>They ended up getting treated as scum...</i>

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.760
<i>The world is cruel...</i>

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:38.930
You're overthinking something 
again, aren't you?

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:42.390
Oh, the racetrack.

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:44.620
You've done enough for today.

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:45.460
Sorry!

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.320
I'll come again tomorrow after classes!

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.030
1 Day until the Ezonoo Festival

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.030
It's finally tomorrow!

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:51.230
<b>Ooezo Agricultural High School Festival</b>

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:07.670
Ooezo 
Nouko

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:10.630
<b>Cow Beauty 
Pageant</b>

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:26.590
Wow! Amazing!

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.030
It's really coming together!

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:31.140
You've been getting up early
 and working hard every day.

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:32.780
You are absolutely ready.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:43.920
The racetrack's done!

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:48.360
Wow!

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:49.770
We really did it!

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:53.960
All right.

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:55.720
Guess I'll go home and have a drink.

00:15:56.200 --> 00:16:00.060
I'm sorry you got dragged 
into our insane plan.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:02.480
Thank you!

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.830
Eh, don't worry about it.

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:07.840
Grown-ups like to have fun, 
too, you know?

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:11.770
Ezonoo Festival 
 9/30 (Day 1)  10/1 (Day 2)  
 12:00~ Jumping   12:00~ Jumping

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:11.780
Tomorrow's the day!

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:13.550
I'm really looking forward to it.

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:15.840
I love the excitement before festivals.

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:17.620
You guys don't have to jump,

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:18.730
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:18.730
so you don't have to worry.

00:16:18.730 --> 00:16:22.150
<i>this might be the longest I've 
gone without studying...</i>

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.520
Uh, what're you doing?

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:28.310
I'm reviewing festival plans.

00:16:28.310 --> 00:16:29.570
I'm just worried.

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:30.990
Wow, so detailed!

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:33.260
You really like studying, Hachiken-kun.

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:36.420
There's always a right answer 
for things like math.

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:39.550
It's fun to work toward that 
answer using equations, isn't it?

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:41.200
But for stuff like Japanese,

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:44.390
there are questions without a right answer,

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:46.660
like "what was the character 
thinking at this time?"

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:47.980
Isn't that one about figuring out

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:50.050
what the person who made 
the question's getting at?

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:51.540
There are hints everywhere,

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:52.530
so it's easy to figure out.

00:16:53.270 --> 00:16:55.700
But I'm not good at it...

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.920
Well, I guess you wouldn't be.

00:16:57.920 --> 00:16:58.660
What?!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:16:59.950
What do you mean, Senpai?

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:02.880
Hachiken, good luck.

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:03.510
Huh?!

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:05.210
Wh-Wh-Wh-What are you getting at, Senpai?

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:08.670
All good to go.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:11.760
Hachiken-kun, what are you doing?

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:12.680
Oh, hey.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:15.900
I was checking the racetrack.

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:17.710
You're such a worry wart.

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:20.060
Though that's why I'm here, too.

00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:23.390
You'll be riding a huge horse.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:25.180
Once the festival's over,

00:17:25.180 --> 00:17:27.590
you should rest up and decompress.

00:17:27.590 --> 00:17:29.520
You've got dark circles under your eyes.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:30.770
Right...

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:32.560
Decompress...

00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:34.790
Maybe I'll go somewhere to have fun.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:38.560
Yeah, I did put in a lot of effort!

00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:41.910
Hachiken, good luck.

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:44.090
Mikage.

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:44.920
What?

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:47.250
A-A-After the festival's over,

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:48.840
w-want to go somewhere and have fun?

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:50.850
Oh, you know!

00:17:50.850 --> 00:17:54.330
You've been getting up early every morning
and training hard for the race!

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:56.720
You placed third in the 
competition earlier, too!

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:59.250
So I want to do it to say 
"good job" and "congrats"!

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:01.600
My treat! Let's go somewhere fun!

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:04.100
Oh, then let's go with 
the rest of the club...

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.320
Just the two of us!

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:06.850
The two. Of us.

00:18:07.430 --> 00:18:09.180
Your treat? Really?

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.150
Yay! I'll go!

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:21.480
Come!

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:32.090
<b>Girls' Dorm</b>

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:30.960
He asked you to come have fun with him?

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.090
Just the two of you?!

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:33.290
Yeah.

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:34.520
A-ha.

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:36.950
So you guys are finally an item.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:38.680
Huh? We're not dating.

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:40.910
You two are going somewhere 
to have fun, right?

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:41.850
Yeah.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:43.460
And you're not dating?

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:44.810
We're friends.

00:18:46.070 --> 00:18:47.140
You're so clueless!

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:48.680
I feel sorry for Hachiken!

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:50.430
Huh? What?

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:51.940
And he's trying so hard 
to send obvious signals...

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:56.090
If a guy and girl of a certain age 
 go out to have fun together,

00:18:56.090 --> 00:18:57.320
that's what it means.

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:03.900
B-B-B-But, if you think about my future,

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:06.510
I come with baggage like 
cows, fields, and old people!

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:07.980
Why would he want someone like me—

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:07.980
Huh?!

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:09.770
<i>That's</i> what you were thinking?!

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:12.580
You should just date people you 
like when you're still a student.

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:14.910
What's your take, Aki?

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:18.170
Isn't he a good catch if you need 
a husband for the Mikage Ranch?

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:21.540
A second son from a normal family? 
That's a great pedigree!

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:25.180
I'm not sure I like all this talk
about catches and pedigrees.

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:30.640
I think it seems rude and impersonal.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:32.970
Aki, you're so serious.

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:35.360
Keep talking like that, and he'll 
have a change of heart on you.

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:38.430
What about you, Yoshino? You guys 
were rumored to be an item before.

00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:40.280
His pedigree is good,

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.110
but I think he's too much work!

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:44.120
He spends way too much time 
overthinking every little thing!

00:19:50.220 --> 00:19:54.050
<i>I wonder if I've been 
holding myself back...</i>

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:57.420
<i>Maybe I can just go with the flow.</i>

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:04.180
<i>Crap!</i>

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:07.730
<i>Now I don't know how to 
act around him tomorrow!</i>

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:14.640
Morning!

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:16.110
Let's go on a walk!

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:23.490
<i>Even grown-ups got all into 
it and got all this made.</i>

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:35.300
<i>I put on some muscle.</i>

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:38.060
<i>The skin on my butt is peeling 
from riding horses, too...</i>

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:43.650
<i>Although, I guess the callus I've always 
had from studying hasn't changed...</i>

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:50.030
Vice Prez,

00:20:50.630 --> 00:20:52.550
I've changed, right?

00:20:52.550 --> 00:20:54.900
Running away here was the 
right thing... right?

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:00.690
All right, let's go back!

00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:03.480
The day of the festival's here!

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:06.090
I'm gonna make it a success!

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:50.430
This story is a work of fiction.
